{"source":"user-event","type":"click","text":"C\n    \n      Layered — Merge Within Domain, Link Across\n      Entities are merged within the same domain. Across domains, a lightweight cross_domain_link edge connects related entities — not a merge, but a signal. The Apply pipeline decides whether to traverse it.\n      \n        Pros\n          Best of both: precision within domain, serendipity across\n          Cross-domain links are cheap (no LLM, just embedding similarity)\n          Apply pipeline controls the blast radius per query\n        \n        Cons\n          Two-tier resolution adds complexity\n          Must define \"same domain\" clearly\n          \"Related across domains\" threshold needs tuning","choice":"c","id":null,"timestamp":1774575555405}
